WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.871
A parcel claim starts with photographs someone else can check.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:12.726
Capture Loop keeps the full label, asks for a useful closer view, and links a confirmed field to both originals.

00:00:12.726 --> 00:00:17.778
This is the working OpenCV five and AWS application.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.850
Start the two-view sample.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:30.481
The agent calls the private AWS image tool, checks the document boundary and page focus, then opens field review.

00:00:30.481 --> 00:00:35.850
The small printed code has only eighty-seven by twenty-five source pixels.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.507
We keep that full-label context and request a closer detail.

00:00:42.266 --> 00:00:45.692
First, a deliberate wrong-photo control.

00:00:45.692 --> 00:00:49.166
I upload a separate parcel as the detail.

00:00:49.166 --> 00:00:53.166
OpenCV finds too little corresponding print.

00:00:53.166 --> 00:00:57.310
The agent asks for another view with surrounding marks.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:03.008
The full label stays selected, and the next upload carries this request forward.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.262
Now load the paired detail.

00:01:07.262 --> 00:01:14.130
OpenCV matches features, checks the target coverage, and maps the field into the new original.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.130
The agent opens a fresh review.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:25.196
The target now occupies one hundred seventy-one by forty-seven source pixels, about twice the linear sampling.

00:01:25.196 --> 00:01:29.235
This controlled pair comes from one licensed photograph.

00:01:30.994 --> 00:01:36.380
Compare the two crops, enter the visible form code, and confirm the field.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.288
This reviewer entry is scripted.

00:01:39.288 --> 00:01:46.538
The saved review identifies both originals, both field crops, and the selected readability response.

00:01:46.538 --> 00:01:51.959
Export the session to inspect the measurements and the actual native tool calls.

00:01:53.914 --> 00:01:56.182
Here is the architecture.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:02:00.656
Whole-label measurements run in private AWS Lambda.

00:02:00.656 --> 00:02:04.985
Field mapping runs in the station with OpenCV five.

00:02:04.985 --> 00:02:09.840
The model receives numerical observations and prior requests.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.235
Its next tool either requests a retake or opens review.

00:02:14.235 --> 00:02:19.971
Executable checks govern both actions, and people supply the field values.

00:02:21.946 --> 00:02:29.582
The report separates selected parcel checks, controlled scale experiments, and natural handheld-video frames.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:36.701
Missing targets, weak correspondence, and insufficient sampling each have a recorded recovery path.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:40.569
Independent phone feedback is the next field test.

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:49.464
Team Blucca combines the owner's account and submission responsibilities with autonomous AI research, engineering, and documentation.

00:02:49.464 --> 00:02:53.569
Try the live station and send one useful capture note.

